  "text": "Designing a reliable file backup system requires a shift in mindset from \"backing up\" to \"ensuring recoverability.\" A backup is only successful if it can be restored. The following is a comprehensive architectural guide to building a resilient backup infrastructure.\n\n---\n\n### 1. The Core Strategy: The 3-2-1 Rule\nBefore implementing specific technologies, adhere to the **3-2-1 Backup Rule**, which is the industry standard for data resilience:\n*   **3 Copies of Data:** Your original data plus two backups.\n*   **2 Different Media Types:** Store backups on two different types of storage",
